From d336edc8c4d373530a8c492f7fccfcb0383fd3d5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vitaly Lipatov <lav@etersoft.ru>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 11:43:40 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 08/16] soc: qcom: enable TCL RPMh power and clock suppliers

Port the ACPI9 implementation to vanilla v7.2.4. Affected ARM64 objects build with W=1. Keep upstream GLINK endpoint removal and reserved-memory resource handling. Full build and hardware validation are separate gates; this commit does not claim hardware validation.
---
 drivers/clk/qcom/clk-rpmh.c             | 22 +++++++++-
 drivers/pmdomain/qcom/rpmhpd.c          | 25 ++++++++++--
 drivers/regulator/qcom-rpmh-regulator.c | 54 ++++++++++++++++++++++---
 drivers/soc/qcom/cmd-db.c               | 21 +++++++---
 drivers/soc/qcom/qcom_aoss.c            | 37 +++++++++--------
 drivers/soc/qcom/rmtfs_mem.c            | 33 ++++++++++-----
 drivers/soc/qcom/rpmh-rsc.c             | 34 ++++++++--------
 7 files changed, 169 insertions(+), 57 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/clk/qcom/clk-rpmh.c b/drivers/clk/qcom/clk-rpmh.c
index 6367b2a5a..8ed17f2ae 100644
